menu "Common Hardware Interfaces"

config OPENEMBER_COMPONENT_HARDWARE
    bool "Build component: Hardware common interfaces"
    default y
    help
      Build lightweight C++ hardware domain primitives such as Result, Error,
      Timestamp, DeviceStatus, and lifecycle states. This component does not
      depend on Link, Protobuf, services, or concrete hardware packages.

endmenu

menu "Sensor Framework"

config OPENEMBER_COMPONENT_SENSOR
    bool "Build component: Sensor Framework"
    default y
    depends on OPENEMBER_COMPONENT_HARDWARE
    help
      Build typed C++ sensor interfaces such as IImu, ITemperatureSensor, IGnss,
      plus mock sensor implementations for CI and no-hardware development.

config OPENEMBER_SENSOR_YESENSE
    bool "YESENSE YIS321 IMU driver (LPIO)"
    default n
    depends on OPENEMBER_COMPONENT_SENSOR
    help
      Requires Linux; uses OpenEmber LPIO and the built-in Yesense decoder.
      Builds only; device selection and UART settings belong to device.yaml.

endmenu

menu "Actuator Framework"

config OPENEMBER_COMPONENT_ACTUATOR
    bool "Build component: Actuator Framework"
    default y
    depends on OPENEMBER_COMPONENT_HARDWARE
    help
      Build typed C++ actuator interfaces such as IActuator and
      IJointController, plus MockJointController for no-hardware development
      and runtime supervision tests.

endmenu
